---
id: org.dxos.spec.deus
name: Deus
version: 0.1.0
---

The spec for `@dxos/deus` itself: the tooling around the `.mdl` language. The language is defined
in `lang/` and motivated in `docs/DESIGN.md`. This document covers what the package must do, so far
only for the spec changelog.

## Extensions

| Term       | URI                          |
| ---------- | ---------------------------- |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`      |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`  |

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Attributed decision log
  A spec carries a `## Changelog` of `decision` blocks (`lang/changelog.mdl`) that traces how it
  came to say what it says, with decisions made by people kept apart from decisions made by agents.

  req F-1.1: Each decision names exactly one decider in `by:`, typed `user:<handle>` (GitHub username or email) or `agent:<name>`.
  req F-1.2: An agent is named by its harness, never by the model that served it.
  req F-1.3: An `agent:` decision names the person it acted for in `for:`; a `user:` decision has no `for:`.
  req F-1.4: A `user:` decision restates what the person said: references resolved, context included and wording fixed, with no information added or removed.
  req F-1.5: The log is append-only. A reversal is a new decision with `supersedes: D-n`.
  req F-1.6: Decision ids are `D-1`, `D-2`, … in the order appended, newest last.
  req F-1.7: Approval of agent decisions is a new `user:` decision whose prose says what it approves.
  req F-1.8: A decision records a choice about the specified system. How the authors worked on the spec or its code (which tool or skill, how the spec is shared, which PR a change goes in, that the document exists or has diagrams) is not a decision.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Every spec change adds a decision
  req F-2.1: A change to a spec outside `## Changelog` adds at least one new decision.
  req F-2.2: A new spec starts with at least one decision.
  req F-2.3: `deus changelog check` enforces F-1.5, F-1.6, F-2.1 and F-2.2 by comparing each changed `.mdl` file with the merge base, and runs in CI as "Check spec changelogs".
  req F-2.4: Language definitions (`lang/`), review rules (`rules/`) and test fixtures are not specs and are exempt.
  req F-2.5: Only `decision` blocks under `## Changelog` form the log; examples elsewhere are ignored.
  req F-2.6: A trivial edit needs no decision: whitespace, or at most 3 words each fixed by an edit distance of at most a third of the word, where no changed word has a digit or is a normative word.
  req F-2.7: A `Spec-Changelog-Skip: <reason>` trailer on any branch commit waives F-2.1 for that branch; the append-only rules still apply.
  req F-2.8: A change with no spec decision behind it, such as adding a diagram or reorganizing sections, carries the F-2.7 trailer instead of a process decision.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Linting
  req F-3.1: The editor linter and `deus lint` report decisions that break F-1.1 or F-1.3.
  req F-3.2: `deus lint --only <source>` restricts output to one check, so the block-type check (which knows only built-in types) does not hide decision errors.
  req F-3.3: `.agents/skills/mdl/scripts/check-decisions.ts` asks TypeSafe System One whether each decision a branch adds breaks F-1.8, giving it the spec's name and introduction so a spec whose system is itself a process is judged on that system. A probability of 0.8 or more fails. It runs in CI as "Check spec decisions" and passes with a notice when `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` is not set.
  req F-3.4: Each block has its own ```` ```mdl ```` fence. The editor linter and `deus lint` report a second block header inside one fence as an `mdl/block` error: a line after the fence's first line, at column 0, whose first word is a built-in block type or a term in the document's `## Extensions` table.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Agent guidance
  req F-4.1: The repo has an `mdl` skill (`.agents/skills/mdl/SKILL.md`) for writing specs and recording decisions.
  req F-4.2: The skill tells an agent to record a person's input first, faithfully — adding context, never assumptions — and its own additions as separate decisions.
  req F-4.3: The skill tells an agent where to read the person's handle from the environment, so it never asks or guesses.
  req F-4.4: The skill tells an agent to leave process out of the changelog (F-1.8), including a person's process instructions, and to run `check-decisions.ts` before committing.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Command-line interface
  req F-5.1: `@dxos/deus` ships one `deus` CLI, built with Effect CLI, and every `.mdl` tool in the repo that belongs to Deus is a subcommand of it: `changelog check`, `lint`, `qa list`, `qa lint` and `review items|check`.
  req F-5.2: The command tree is exported from `@dxos/deus/cli`, and the `dx` CLI mounts it as `dx deus`.
  req F-5.3: `pnpm deus` runs the CLI from source with plain `node` at the repo root, so CI and agents need no build.
  req F-5.4: `qa list` prints the numbered `test` and `suite` blocks that `/dxos:qa` addresses; `qa lint` reports references a test never binds and teardowns that could remove an object the run did not create.
  req F-5.5: `review items` lists every item a spec review must judge; `review check` validates a `.review.mdl` against its spec and the checkout.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: SQL tables
  req F-6.1: The `table` block (`lang/sql.mdl`, `org.dxos.mdl.table@1.0`) declares a SQL table a component owns: its columns with SQLite storage classes and SQL constraints, its keys and indexes, and the migration set it lives in.
  req F-6.2: A `table` states the schema after the spec's changes; `new:` marks the table or the columns the spec adds.
  req F-6.3: A `table` is a spec item that requirements cite as `table:<name>` or `table:<name>.<column>`, and `deus lint` knows the block type.
  req F-6.4: A spec refers to code by component or symbol name and to another spec by its frontmatter `id`, never by file path; a `table` names its store and migration-history table, not a migrations directory.
  req F-6.5: A `table` is part of the spec's data model: the viewer's Data model view shows it as a stored root with its columns as fields, its store as a tag, and a `REFERENCES <table>(<column>)` column as a reference to that table.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Spec dependencies
  req F-7.1: A spec declares each spec it builds on in its body, never its frontmatter: one core `uses` block per spec under `## Dependencies`, after the opening prose and before `## Extensions`, whose required one-line prose says what it takes from that spec.
  req F-7.2: A plugin spec's `plugin` block lists the plugin's runtime dependencies in `dependsOn` (plugin dialect 1.1), exactly as `dx.config.ts` declares them. An id in `dependsOn` is never repeated under `uses`; a spec's dependencies are the union of both.
  req F-7.3: A reference into another spec is `<spec id>#<item>`, where the item is a block id or `req` id of that spec. It is recognised in prose and anywhere in an `mdl` block; other code fences are not scanned. A `github:` key into a `.mdl` file is not a reference.
  req F-7.4: `deus index` maps every tracked `.mdl` spec's frontmatter id to its path and items, leaving out spec reviews, test fixtures and the illustrative `lang/examples/`. Two files with one id is an error reported on both.
  req F-7.5: The editor linter and `deus lint` report, as `mdl/ref` and `mdl/uses` errors: a reference to an unknown spec or item, a reference to a spec outside the dependencies, a `github:` key into a `.mdl` file outside `## Changelog`, an unknown, repeated or self dependency, and an id in both `dependsOn` and `uses`. Dependency cycles are allowed, and dependencies are not transitive.
  req F-7.6: `deus review check` judges a `plugin` block's `dependsOn` against `dx.config.ts`; a plugin in one and not the other is valid only under a `diverged` verdict.
  req F-7.7: The spec index of the dxos repository is generated at build time and bundled with plugin-code. The spec viewer opens a referenced spec scrolled to the item (to the top for a bare id), and draws a reference it cannot resolve as a broken link with the lint message on hover.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Showcases
  req F-8.1: The `showcase` block (`lang/showcase.mdl`, `org.dxos.mdl.showcase@1.0`) links features of a spec to a recorded example of them: the presentation a pull request produced when it implemented them. It is the spec-file counterpart of plugin-projects' `Demonstrates` relation, which links the same presentation to the same features in a space.
  req F-8.2: A showcase is non-normative; it is not a spec item, and a spec review does not judge it.
  req F-8.3: A `showcase` names the `feat` and `req` ids it shows in `for:`, and `deus lint` reports one that names none or names an id the document does not declare.
  req F-8.4: A showcase carries its pull request and media as URLs, never a file path; its deck is located from its id.
```

## Changelog

Backfilled on 2026-10-20 from the session that built the changelog,
https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093.

```mdl
decision D-1: `.mdl` specs get a changelog section: a log of authoritative decisions, each tagged with the person (by username or email) or the agent that made it. Its goal is to trace how decisions were made, and to keep decisions by people separate from decisions by agents.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The repo has an `mdl` skill.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.1]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The changelog is a `decision` block type in a new dialect, `lang/changelog.mdl`. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  why: Every other construct in the language is an `ext`-defined block in a dialect file; a dialect keeps the changelog opt-in per document.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A decider is `user:<handle>` or `agent:<name>`, and an agent is named by its harness, not its model. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2]
  why: A typed prefix makes "which decisions did a person make" a filter, and the linter can reject untyped entries. Models change mid-session; the name must stay stable across the log.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: An agent decision names the person it acted for in `for:`. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.3]
  why: An agent decides within latitude a person gave it; the trace is incomplete without whose.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The log is append-only with monotonic `D-n` ids; reversals use `supersedes:`. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.5, F-1.6]
  why: An edited entry erases the trace the log exists to keep.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: A person endorsing an agent decision is recorded as `ratified-by:` on that entry, the only edit an entry admits. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Only decisions that change what the spec requires are logged; edits, renames and reformatting are not. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  why: Read from "authoritative decisions" in [D-1]; git already records edits.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Decision attribution is linted in the editor and by `scripts/lint-mdl.ts`, whose `--only` flag isolates one check.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3]
  why: The existing block-type check knows only built-in types and flags valid dialect blocks, so a CLI without a filter is unusable on real specs.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Specs are usually written by people and agents together: the person gives coarse ideas and the agent fills in the gaps. Knowledge from each goes in separate decision entries. The agent first records a faithful representation of what the person wrote, adding only context and no assumptions, then records its own additions as separate decisions. A person approving an agent's design is a decision of its own. These rules go in the `mdl` skill.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.7, F-4.2]
  supersedes: D-7
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Every change to a spec adds a decision. How to enforce this mechanically is to be worked out.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2]
  supersedes: D-8
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Approval is not a separate kind of entry, as the proposed `approves:` field would have made it; an approval is the same entry as any other decision, and its prose says what it approves.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.7]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-13: A `user:` decision may carry `quote:` (verbatim words) and `context:` (added facts); an agent decision may not carry `quote:`. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.4]
  why: Separate fields keep the person's words apart from what the recording agent added, so "faithful" can be checked by reading.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: `scripts/check-changelog.ts` enforces [D-11] in CI by diffing each changed `.mdl` against the merge base, and also rejects edited, removed, reordered or out-of-sequence entries. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3]
  why: A diff against the base is the only place "this change added no decision" is visible; the same diff checks append-only for free. Placed beside the changesets check, which works the same way.
  rejected:
    - A Claude Stop hook alone: only covers agent sessions on the Claude harness, not human edits or other harnesses.
    - A husky pre-commit hook: skippable, and not run in the cloud sandbox.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Language definitions, review rules and test fixtures are exempt from [D-11], and only decisions under `## Changelog` count as the log. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.4, F-2.5]
  why: These `.mdl` files are not specs of a component; `lang/changelog.mdl` itself shows example decisions that must not be read as its log.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: If Deus has no spec of its own, it gets one, backfilled from the session that built the changelog.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-17: An agent should know from the environment who it is speaking to. The `mdl` skill says how to find the person's identity, so the next agent does not stumble on it.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.3]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-18: Read the handle from the session's GitHub account first, then the harness's stated user, then local `git config`. Fills in [D-17].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.3]
  why: The GitHub login is the preferred handle form (F-1.1). In the cloud sandbox `git config` names the agent, not the person.
```

```mdl
decision D-19: The changelog check tolerates small "type" changes, so they can go through without a decision.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.6]
  supersedes: D-11
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-20: The mdl skill documents an escape hatch from the every-change-adds-a-decision rule.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.7, F-4]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-21: "Small type changes" in [D-19] means typo fixes. A trivial edit is whitespace, or at most 3 changed words, each within an edit distance of a third of its length (adjacent swaps count once), with no digits and no normative word on either side. Fills in [D-19].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.6]
  why: Typos are short, local, and leave the word count unchanged. Ids, numbers and words like must/most or can/can't change meaning in one letter. Existing decisions get no tolerance, because the log is append-only.
  rejected:
    - A fixed distance of 2 for every word: lets one-letter words such as X and Y swap.
```

```mdl
decision D-22: The escape hatch is a `Spec-Changelog-Skip: <reason>` commit trailer that lifts only the missing-decision rule for the branch. Fills in [D-20].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.7]
  why: Same shape as the changesets waiver; the reason is kept in git history, and append-only stays enforced.
  rejected:
    - A PR label: not visible to a local run of the script, and leaves no reason in history.
```

```mdl
decision D-23: An unclosed `decision` block, as while typing, ends at the next fence or at the end of the text.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.1]
  why: The editor linter otherwise reported a missing `by:`, or read the next block's fields. Raised by the CodeRabbit review.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093#discussion_r4321642968
```

```mdl
decision D-24: A person's input is not quoted verbatim, because prompts are messy and lack context. The agent restates it and may resolve references, include context and fix wording, but must not add or remove information.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.4, F-4.2]
  supersedes: D-13
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-25: Drop the `quote:` and `context:` fields and their lint rule; the restatement lives in the entry's prose. Fills in [D-24].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.4, F-3.1]
  why: With no verbatim quote, a separate context field only splits one restatement in two.
```

```mdl
decision D-26: Just this once, the earlier decisions are cleaned up: D-1, D-2, D-10, D-11, D-12, D-16 and D-17 were rewritten to the restated form of [D-24], without `quote:` or `context:`. The log is append-only again from here.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.5]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-27: Decisions about process rather than the spec do not belong in a changelog. The `mdl` skill says so, and the mdl lint tooling enforces it mechanically with a System One check.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.8, F-3.3, F-4.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-28: `check-decisions.ts` judges only the decisions a branch adds, one System One `noul` question each, with the spec's name and introduction in the state; 0.8 or more fails, and a missing key skips with a notice. Fills in [D-27].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.3]
  why: Calibrated on the 84 decisions in the repo's specs and an EDGE spec with two known process entries (0.95, 0.96). Without the introduction, 26 of the 84 were flagged, most in this spec, whose system is the changelog process; with it, 6 score 0.7 or more and 3 score 0.8 or more. Judging only new decisions keeps the log append-only.
  rejected:
    - A keyword or regex rule (process wording varies too much to match).
    - Re-judging every existing decision in CI (it would demand edits to append-only entries).
```

```mdl
decision D-29: A spec change with no spec decision behind it carries the `Spec-Changelog-Skip` trailer rather than a process decision. Fills in [D-27].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.8]
  why: F-2.1 otherwise forces a decision for a diagram or a reorganized section, and the only decision available would be a process one.
```

```mdl
decision D-30: All `.mdl` tooling is grouped under one formal `deus` CLI built with Effect CLI, in `@dxos/deus`. The standalone scripts become its subcommands and keep their behaviour and flags. The command tree is exported from a package subpath so that the `dx` CLI mounts it as `dx deus`. Every caller moves to the new commands, with no compatibility shims.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5, F-2.3, F-3.1, F-3.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-31: The subcommands are `changelog check` (was `scripts/check-changelog.ts`), `lint` (was `scripts/lint-mdl.ts`), `qa list` (was the dxos plugin's `scripts/list-tests.mjs`), `qa lint` (was `tools/qa-lint/*`) and `review items|check` (was the spec-review skill's `scripts/review.mts`). The agentic-review scripts and the mdl skill's `check-decisions.ts` stay in their skills. Fills in [D-30].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.1, F-5.4, F-5.5]
  why: The five tools parse only Deus documents and need nothing beyond node; agentic-review and `check-decisions.ts` call the System One API, and agentic-review owns a review store.
```

```mdl
decision D-32: `pnpm deus` runs `bin/deus.ts` with `node --conditions=source`, and `deus qa list` skips `__fixtures__` directories. Fills in [D-30].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.3, F-5.4]
  why: CI runs the changelog check before anything is built. Grammar fixtures carry example tests that are not runnable plans, the same trap the dialect exclusion already avoids.
```

```mdl
decision D-33: Deus has a block type for SQL tables.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6]
```

```mdl
decision D-34: The block is `table` in a new `lang/sql.mdl` dialect, with `store`, `columns`, `key`, `unique`, `indexes` and `new`; columns use SQLite storage classes, `?` for nullable, and SQL constraints. Fills in [D-33].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6.1, F-6.2, F-6.3]
  why: Every SQL store in the repo is SQLite with numbered migrations, so the storage classes and the migration directory say exactly what the DDL says; `new:` lets a review check that a migration adds what the spec promises.
  rejected:
    - "Extend `db` from the standard dialect: it describes a whole persistence layer and has no field definition to extend."
```

```mdl
decision D-35: Specs do not specify file paths.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-36: A spec names a component or symbol for code and a frontmatter `id` for another spec; a `table`'s `store:` is the database and its migration-history table. Diagram `ref=` attributes keep their paths, since they are checking metadata for the renderer, not prose. Fills in [D-35].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6.1, F-6.4]
  why: Names survive a move and are what a reader searches for; the migration-history table identifies a migration set as exactly as its directory.
```

```mdl
decision D-37: A `table` contributes to the data model.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-38: A table is always a stored root; its columns are its fields and a `REFERENCES` column is a reference edge to the named table. Fills in [D-37].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6.5]
  why: A table is persisted by definition, and a foreign key is the SQL form of the `Ref<…>` field that makes a `type` reference another.
```

```mdl
decision D-39: A spec's dependencies on other specs are declared in its body, not in its frontmatter.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-40: A plugin spec lists the plugins it depends on in a field of the plugin dialect, and any spec lists the specs it builds on in a core Dependencies section.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.1, F-7.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-41: A dependency is never declared twice: a plugin listed in the plugin dialect's field is not repeated in the Dependencies section.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-42: A reference into another spec is fully qualified as `<spec id>#<item>`.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-43: A reference to a spec that is not among the spec's dependencies is a lint error.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-44: The spec viewer opens a referenced spec scrolled to the referenced item.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.7]
```

```mdl
decision D-45: Existing `github:` keys into `.mdl` files are converted to `<spec id>#<item>` references, and lint rejects such keys.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.3, F-7.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-46: A plugin's `dependsOn` is exactly its runtime dependencies as `dx.config.ts` declares them, and every other spec it builds on goes under `uses`. A review that finds a plugin in one and not the other judges it `diverged`.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.2, F-7.6]
```

```mdl
decision D-47: The viewer's spec index is generated at build time and bundled with plugin-code. It covers the dxos repository only; another repository gets its own index later, and until then its specs cannot reference dxos specs.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.7]
```

```mdl
decision D-48: The spec index leaves out `*.review.mdl` files and test fixtures. Fills in [D-42].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.4]
  why: A review and a fixture are not specs a reference can name, and fixtures reuse ids on purpose.
```

```mdl
decision D-49: Deus owns the spec index: lint builds it from the checkout and the build emits the same index for the viewer. Fills in [D-43] and [D-47].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.4, F-7.7]
  why: One builder means lint and the viewer cannot disagree about what an id resolves to.
```

```mdl
decision D-50: The core block is `uses`, one per dependency, and `## Dependencies` sits after the opening prose and before `## Extensions`. Fills in [D-40].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.1]
  why: A reader learns what the spec is before what it builds on, and the declarations precede the block types they may need.
```

```mdl
decision D-51: A `uses` block's one-line prose, saying why the dependency exists, is required. Fills in [D-40].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.1]
  why: An id alone does not tell a reader what this spec takes from the other.
```

```mdl
decision D-52: The plugin dialect's field is `dependsOn`, named as in `dx.config.ts`. Fills in [D-40].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.2]
  why: One name for one concept in the config and the spec makes the review comparison obvious.
```

```mdl
decision D-53: The plugin dialect moves to version 1.1 for `dependsOn`. Fills in [D-40].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.2]
  why: The field is optional and additive, so existing plugin blocks stay valid: a minor bump.
```

```mdl
decision D-54: The editor linter and `deus lint` share the reference diagnostics, under the sources `mdl/ref` (references and keys) and `mdl/uses` (declarations). Fills in [D-43] and [D-45].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.5]
  why: Shared checks keep the editor and CI in step, and two sources let `--only` select either.
```

```mdl
decision D-55: A dependency cycle is allowed. Fills in [D-43].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.5]
  why: Specs can legitimately describe each other, as a host and the engine it embeds do.
```

```mdl
decision D-56: The viewer draws an unresolvable reference as a broken link, with the lint message on hover. Fills in [D-44].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.7]
  why: The reader sees the break where it is, with the same explanation lint gives.
```

```mdl
decision D-57: References are recognised in prose and anywhere inside an `mdl` block, `#` comments included; any other code fence is not scanned. Fills in [D-42].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.3]
  why: An ASCII diagram or a code example can show a reference without declaring a dependency, while spec text is always checked.
```

```mdl
decision D-58: Approve [D-48], [D-49], [D-50], [D-51], [D-52], [D-53], [D-54], [D-55], [D-56] and [D-57].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-59: The spec index also leaves out `lang/examples/`. Fills in [D-48].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.4]
  why: The examples are successive versions of one illustrative chess spec and share its id, so indexing them reports a duplicate on every file.
```

```mdl
decision D-60: A `github:` key into a `.mdl` file inside `## Changelog` is not reported. Fills in [D-45].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.5]
  why: The changelog is append-only, so a decision written before references existed cannot be rewritten to satisfy the rule.
  rejected:
    - Rewriting such decisions, which `deus changelog check` rejects as an edit to the log.
```

```mdl
decision D-61: In a reference, the spec id's segments after the first may be camelCase. Fills in [D-42].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7.3]
  why: Plugin ids such as `org.dxos.plugin.fileSystem` are camelCase, and a lowercase-only grammar never recognised a reference into them.
```

```mdl
decision D-62: Approve [D-59], [D-60] and [D-61].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-63: Each block gets its own ```` ```mdl ```` fence, and a second block header inside one fence is a lint error. Every existing multi-block fence in the repo's specs is split into one block per fence.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-64: A block header inside a fence is a line after the fence's first line, at column 0, of the form `<type> [<id>][: <title>]`, whose type is a built-in block type or a term in the document's `## Extensions` table. Fills in [D-63].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.4]
  why: A block body is always indented, so a column-0 line of a known type is never body text; on the repo's specs this finds exactly the hidden headers and no prose line.
  rejected:
    - Any column-0 line of the header form, which would also flag undeclared types such as `surface` lines that list surfaces.
```

```mdl
decision D-65: When a pull request merges, the presentation it produced stays with the features it implemented, as the non-normative part of the spec: examples of the feature, not requirements of it.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-8.1, F-8.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-66: The link is a `showcase` block in a new `lang/showcase.mdl` dialect, with `for`, `pr`, `video`, `image` and `note`; `deus lint` checks that `for:` cites only feat and req ids the document declares. Fills in [D-65].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8.1, F-8.3]
  why: A block of its own keeps examples out of the requirement text that reviews judge, and one feature can gather several showcases over time; checking `for:` keeps a renamed feature from orphaning its examples.
  rejected:
    - "A `showcase:` field on `feat`: it mixes examples into the normative block and holds only one value cleanly."
```

```mdl
decision D-67: A showcase names its pull request and media by URL, and its deck lives beside the spec as `showcase/<SC-n>.md`, so the spec names no path. Fills in [D-65] and [D-35].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8.4]
  why: URLs outlive a move of the package, and deriving the deck's location from the id keeps [D-35] without losing the deck.
```

```mdl
decision D-68: A `showcase` block is the spec-file counterpart of plugin-projects' `Demonstrates` relation: the same deck, imported into a space with `CreateShowcase`, is linked to the same features there. Fills in [D-65].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8.1]
  why: A showcase is a presenter deck linked to features by `Demonstrates` in a space, so the repository side names that link rather than a second kind of showcase.
```
